<tr><td><strong>Investment</strong></td><td>~$4B, building retrofit, fuel cells, electrical, fire, security, engineering. Stated identically in both decks. Note the itemization excludes compute hardware, which puts infrastructure at ~$16M/MW, a figure that does not reconcile cleanly with fuel cell costs and warrants a line-item capital stack <a class="fnref" href="#fs60"><sup>51</sup></a></td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Jobs</strong></td><td>400–600 construction (deck) / "over a thousand" (testimony); 100–200 permanent at $85–90k+ <a class="fnref" href="#fs60"><sup>51</sup></a></td></tr>
