<p><strong>The Council is being asked to grant a permanent by-right entitlement eighteen days before the air permit that governs the facility can become final, and three days before the public can still demand a hearing on it.</strong><a class="fnref" href="#fs44"><sup>28</sup></a></p>
<div class="callout co-insight">
  <div class="lbl">Ask:</div>
  <p>The applicant's website says the air permit is approved. The state's document is an Intent to Approve dated 4 August, with a comment period open until 5 September and conditions that may still change.<a class="fnref" href="#fs44"><sup>28</sup></a> Why is the city voting on the zoning before the permit is final?</p>
</div>
<p><strong>What the permit actually contains, and it is worth stating fairly.</strong> The facility is permitted as <strong>1,210 Bloom Energy Server 6.5 units, 393.25 MW combined nameplate</strong>, SIC 4911 Electric Services, classified New Minor Source, with no applicable federal standards.<a class="fnref" href="#fs1"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
